/*!
@mainpage CCCC

CCCC (**C**omprehensive **C** **C**ompensation **C**ompiler) compiles C to
bytecode and runs it in a built-in VM. It is a drop-in frontend for `cc`,
`clang` and `gcc`: a compile-time pass between the preprocessor and the parser
runs `[[cccc::comptime]]` functions and expands their results, and
`-c=native` hands the result to a host compiler.

This site documents the public headers. The user guides live in
[docs/](https://github.com/takeiteasy/cccc/tree/trunk/docs).

## Headers

| Header | Use it to | Guide |
|---|---|---|
| @ref building.h "cccc/building.h" | Write `--build` scripts: targets, profiles, cross-compilation | [build](https://github.com/takeiteasy/cccc/blob/trunk/docs/build.md) |
| @ref reflection.h "cccc/reflection.h" | Write comptime macros: inspect, build and quote AST nodes | [macros](https://github.com/takeiteasy/cccc/blob/trunk/docs/macros.md) |
| @ref testing.h "cccc/testing.h" | Write `[[cccc::test]]` tests with the `Assert*` macros | [testing](https://github.com/takeiteasy/cccc/blob/trunk/docs/testing.md) |
| @ref kernel.h "cccc/kernel.h" | Launch `[[cccc::kernel]]` functions over a grid of work-items | [kernels](https://github.com/takeiteasy/cccc/blob/trunk/docs/kernels.md) |
| @ref omp.h "omp.h" | Call the OpenMP runtime API under `-fopenmp` | [openmp](https://github.com/takeiteasy/cccc/blob/trunk/docs/openmp.md) |
| @ref opencl.h "cccc/opencl.h" | Read OpenCL C 1.2 kernels (`.cl`, `-x cl`) onto the kernel model | [opencl](https://github.com/takeiteasy/cccc/blob/trunk/docs/opencl.md) |
| `cccc/derive.h` | Generate serializers, accessors, equality, JSON and more with attributes such as `@serialize` and `@to_json` | [derive](https://github.com/takeiteasy/cccc/blob/trunk/docs/derive.md) |
| `cccc/json.h` | Runtime behind `@to_json` / `@from_json`; include it next to `derive.h` | [derive](https://github.com/takeiteasy/cccc/blob/trunk/docs/derive.md) |

`testing.h`, `building.h` and `opencl.h` are injected automatically in their
modes. `reflection.h` is available to comptime code without an include. `derive.h` and
`json.h` are ordinary includes; they have no generated reference pages, so use
the guide.

## Build scripts

A `build.c` script declares targets with the Builder API of @ref building.h "building.h":
each target is a function returning a `BuildTarget *`, run with
`cccc --build build.c --build-target=<name>`. CCCC's own `build.c` is a working
example, and its `docs` target builds this site.

## Example

```c
@comptime Node *square(Node *x) { return Quote("($1) * ($1)", x); }

int main(void) { return square(6); }   // 36, folded at compile time
```

```sh
cccc demo.c                    # run in the VM
cccc -c=native demo.c -o demo  # lower to C and build with the host compiler
```
*/
